  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'ONE PASSENGER. FOUR TAXIS. NO MANNERS.


    Drive through the blue roadside
    pickup marker. The first qualifying truck collects automatically. Drive through
    the gold destination marker to score. Stopping and interaction menus are never
    required.


    Bump the carrier at a meaningful closing speed to steal the SAME
    passenger and destination. A visible 1.25-second lock prevents contact ping-pong.
    Ordinary traffic, pedestrians and explosions never steal. A destroyed or out-of-bounds
    carrier resets the passenger at a neutral roadside stop; the destination survives.
    Shallow surface water is safe.


    First to five by default. Choose another
    target, five minutes (tied leaders play a sudden-death delivery), or solo practice.
    Global names, colors and controller ownership are retained.


    Use the setup
    or pause VIEW button for shared arena, chase or the actual Taxi cab. Each whole
    controller may switch its own view with NORTH; shared sticks preserve independent
    steering and use the setup view. Keyboard clusters use C, End, F, J for camera.
    Hold and cue the jug using the displayed source bindings, then throw a filled
    jug using the displayed action. Its blast never awards possession. Flip-off is
    a separate action.


    The playable district is the original authored Taxi
    town. Road barriers visibly close the later regional connections. GPS uses its
    actual connected road graph; it never routes through a different district. Offline
    only.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: be1034cebd9fa3643a48d11ef76e4708, type: 2}
